// RULE: F8.4
// RT-234's guard: a generic trait's function as a value with nothing to
// say the trait's arguments (no expected fn type, two impls): refused, as
// rustc's E0283 (type annotations needed), never the first impl's. (A
// later call `h(1)` would decide it in rustc; vole decides at the path.)
// ERROR: error[type.infer]: 'E2' has more than one impl of 'Conv' that gives 'mk'
struct E2 {
    c: i64,
}

trait Conv<X> {
    fn mk(x: X) -> Self;
}

impl Conv<i64> for E2 {
    fn mk(x: i64) -> E2 {
        E2 { c: x }
    }
}

impl Conv<bool> for E2 {
    fn mk(x: bool) -> E2 {
        E2 { c: if x { 1 } else { 0 } }
    }
}

fn main() {
    let h = E2::mk;
    println("{}", 0);
}
